      "body": "## Pull request overview\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Copilot was unable to run its full agentic suite in this review.\n\nAdds an Apple Intel Thunderbolt USB\u2011C xHCI \u201ckeep awake\u201d workaround by installing a udev rule and wiring it into both the installer and migrations.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add a new Apple hardware config script that installs a udev rule for Intel JHL6540 (8086:15d4).\n- Add a migration that applies the same fix via sourcing the config script.\n- Run the new fix as part of the global hardware configuration flow.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 3 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| migrations/1786836656.sh | New migration to apply the Thunderbolt USB\u2011C xHCI wake workaround. |\n| install/config/hardware/apple/fix-tb-usb-wakeup.sh | New installer script that writes a udev rule and triggers it. |\n| install/config/all.sh | Hooks the new Apple workaround into the standard install sequence. |\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/basecamp/omarchy/new/dev?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>",
